                                            "A set of advocates; a barristers' chambers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Scotland"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6da3fe7a-cfff-37f5-b7c4-07547a97698b",
                                        "entry_id": "365b88b7-c920-3606-a055-2921a97de4bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An organization of sumo wrestlers who live and train together."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d8615f5-c474-37a3-b6bc-359f6776c736",
                                        "entry_id": "365b88b7-c920-3606-a055-2921a97de4bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of wrestlers who support each other within a wrestling storyline."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49479b06-ace9-4687-8d6b-eda402fd71cc",
                                                "sense_id": "8d8615f5-c474-37a3-b6bc-359f6776c736",
                                                "text": "Paul, who signed with WWE in late June, appeared in a segment with Reigns' stable, the Bloodline, on Friday's episode of SmackDown after making comments earlier in the week regarding a potential match with the Tribal Chief."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b48f1a1-1083-3794-8df6-c2647d2b6653",
                                        "entry_id": "365b88b7-c920-3606-a055-2921a97de4bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of prostitutes managed by one pimp."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7e3296d-1e38-46f9-8f7d-4a04f73cd300",
                                                "sense_id": "4b48f1a1-1083-3794-8df6-c2647d2b6653",
                                                "text": "My pimp vision enabled me to see that no hoe in my stable would be more worthy of the game than my young turnout red-bones."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "959cd1ea-84aa-39e2-ae23-1309e09ee919",
                                        "entry_id": "365b88b7-c920-3606-a055-2921a97de4bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of people who are looked after, mentored, or trained in one place or for a particular purpose or profession."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78e23050-daef-3ed9-9f57-d81d8c7fc32a",
                                        "entry_id": "365b88b7-c920-3606-a055-2921a97de4bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coherent or consistent set of things (typically abstract) available or presented; array."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecea0a70-8b29-4219-ac14-98ff47872f72",
                                                "sense_id": "78e23050-daef-3ed9-9f57-d81d8c7fc32a",
                                                "text": "This Article argues that to date, the Supreme Court has drawn from a narrow stable of arguments to create a fairly standard, yet coarse, analysis to consider when to apply proximate cause to statutes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "701f90ce-b943-4267-94b4-979510b2d8bd",
                                                "sense_id": "78e23050-daef-3ed9-9f57-d81d8c7fc32a",
                                                "text": "Built into the popular conception of the genius mythos in the sciences is something more than mere intelligence; the solitary free-thinking scientist is also expected to showcase a proclivity for eccentricity, rule breaking, and unconventional thinking and behavior. But when it comes to the abuse of scientific power for sexual predation, this stable of behaviors represents a slippery slope."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "stable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "016c2f4b-faf2-3c48-9e55-2807907f1037",
                                        "entry_id": "132bb607-6a9a-378b-a635-5a637a9ee6c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put or keep (an animal) in a stable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1428c35b-f01f-4f95-9fe2-8f76be9800b3",
                                                "sense_id": "016c2f4b-faf2-3c48-9e55-2807907f1037",
                                                "text": "It is not difficult for the wealthy brewer or pluralist publican, while he takes his ease in his comfortable dwelling on the Lord’s Day, or rolls in his chariot to the house of prayer, to denounce the agitation in favour of Sunday-closing, while his weary barmen and barmaidens “work from early morn to midnight” to carpet his ample halls and stable his well-fed horses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11f36068-6e4c-48f9-84e3-174747b09166",
                                                "sense_id": "016c2f4b-faf2-3c48-9e55-2807907f1037",
                                                "text": "\"I hope your have been quite comfortable.\" ¶ \"Never better stabled in my life,\" said Bree."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a4c6470-d2e3-32d3-bb02-d6999ce8784b",
                                        "entry_id": "132bb607-6a9a-378b-a635-5a637a9ee6c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dwell in a stable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ad285b5-32ed-3279-8b15-42fa9003f3d8",
                                        "entry_id": "132bb607-6a9a-378b-a635-5a637a9ee6c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To park (a rail vehicle)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0e17c8d-2eb6-4beb-9d16-fc089d313826",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad285b5-32ed-3279-8b15-42fa9003f3d8",
                                                "text": "S.R. Pacific No. 34010 Sidmouth leaves Wembley Central to stable the stock of its excursion from the S.R. at North Wembley; the train was run in connection with a Wembley football event on April 30, 1960."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "492e72dc-a4e9-45cb-b040-04a1bef8792b",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad285b5-32ed-3279-8b15-42fa9003f3d8",
                                                "text": "Great Western Railway has placed its Class 143 Pacer fleet into warm storage, with the majority stabled at Exeter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
